            <ArticleTitle>Diffusion-weighted MR imaging in acute spinal cord ischemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2076-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report diffusion-weighted (DW) MR findings for acute spinal cord ischemia in a 56-year-old patient. MR imaging obtained approximately 3 h after symptom onset demonstrated an area of hyperintensity on DW images, but no conspicuous signal abnormality on T2-weighted images in the conus medullaris. DW imaging of the spinal cord can contribute to the early detection of spinal cord vascular compromise.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
